Cactus Code Thorn TestSubcyclingNoRestrict
Author(s)    : Liwei Ji <jiliwei.phys@gmail.com>
Maintainer(s): Liwei Ji <jiliwei.phys@gmail.com>
Licence      : LGPL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Purpose

Regression test for checkpoint recovery under subcycling of an evolved
group with restriction disabled (restrict="no").

Under subcycling, ODESolvers fills the coarse-fine ghosts of every evolved
group on a refined level by dense output from the level's source bands
(the parent's old state and RK stage derivatives), at every stage and at a
virtual end of each substep. When the driver restricts a time-aligned
window that holds the finest level, ProlongateRestrictedGFs overwrites
these ghosts on the levels aligned with their parents, by spatial
prolongation from the restricted parent, but only for groups with
restriction enabled. A group with restrict="no" keeps the dense output.
Recovery must therefore replay the dense output for such a group from the
checkpointed bands, rather than prolongate it from the parent's
checkpointed state.

This thorn is a trimmed copy of TestSubcyclingMC2 (scalar wave equation,
Gaussian initial data, fourth-order centred Laplacian, ODESolvers RK4,
three refinement levels) without the moving box or the added level. It
evolves the same wave twice:

  state    {u, rho}         restricted; error compares it with the
                            analytic solution
  state_nr {u_nr, rho_nr}   restrict="no"; ODESolvers_PostStep applies
                            u_nr = max(u_nr, u_floor) in the interior

The floor makes the parent's tl=0 differ from the dense output its child's
coarse-fine ghosts keep: with a negative amplitude u decreases from zero,
and once it reaches the floor every RK update pushes it below again, so the
floor clips it at every step, also on the coarse cells under the finest
level's coarse-fine ghosts. Prolongating state_nr from the parent at
recovery then differs from the uninterrupted run by far more than the
testsuite tolerance. The floor is idempotent, because ODESolvers_PostStep
also runs at POSTRESTRICT and once more per clock group at
post_recover_variables.

2. Tests

  test/checkpoint-openpmd-midcycle.par
      3 levels, checkpoint at iteration 6, where the clocks are 2, 3/2
      and 3/2 coarse steps: the finest clock group [1,3) is restricted
      and level 2 is aligned with level 1. Runs on to iteration 8 as the
      uninterrupted baseline.
  test/recover-openpmd-midcycle.par
      Recovers that checkpoint and runs to iteration 8; its output must
      equal the baseline's bit for bit.
